8a6y|n|The festival of Saturn, celebrated in December, originally during one day, but afterward during seven days, as a period of unrestrained license and merriment for all classes, extending even to the slaves. ; Hence: A period or occasion of general license, in which the passions or vices have riotous indulgence.	a:5gu1,170,1;8455,89,3~8455,89,3;5gu1,170,1	v:1883,42,4~1883,42,4	n:8455,96,5;4mal,84,4~8455,96,5;4mal,84,4
8a70|a|Of or pertaining to Saturn, whose age or reign, from the mildness and wisdom of his government, is called the golden age. ; Hence: Resembling the golden age; distinguished for peacefulness, happiness, contentment. ; Of or pertaining to the planet Saturn; as, the Saturnian year.	j:5yhq,147,30;5ygb,108,21;mbf,83,2;82lb,69,5;9cla,50,11;5wns,46,5~5yhq,147,30;5ygb,108,21;9cla,50,11;5wns,46,5;82lb,69,5;mbf,83,2
